    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## One template, a whole pool - and proof the pool is actually different\n\nAn LLM writes ONE spintax template from your brief; the Spintax node then generates variants from it forever, offline and free. The interesting half is what comes after.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Your brief goes to **Build Authoring Prompt**, which emits the prompt pair for your own LLM node.\n2. **Validate** routes the draft to Valid or Invalid; on Invalid, **Build Repair Prompt** points the model at the exact offending token and one repair round runs.\n3. **Render Many** turns the valid template into 12 documents.\n4. **Lint** reads each rendered document for defects that live in the combination of choices and never in the template: two slots picking the same word, a space before a comma.\n5. **Uniqueness** reads the surviving pool as a whole, drops near-duplicates and reports a footprint - the share of five-word windows that repeat across it. Measured on real pools of equal size: one template about 0.96, six templates about 0.02.\n\n### Setup\n\n1. Connect credentials on the **OpenAI Chat Model** node, or swap the chain for any LLM node you already use; the Spintax operations exchange plain text and ignore the provider.\n2. Edit **Your brief and product** - the brief and the four values are all in that one node.\n3. Execute. Everything after the LLM is deterministic: same base seed, same twelve documents.\n\n### Customization tips\n\nThe LLM runs once; every later run costs nothing. Put the strings every document repeats - product name, brand, a merge tag - into **Shared Strings**, or the metric measures your product name instead of your writing. Lower **Footprint Limit** to 0.15 to turn the footprint into a gate.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 1000
      },
      "id": "Sticky Note",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -784,
        -96
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 - Author the template\n\nYour brief and the allowed variables become the canonical prompt for your own LLM. `spintaxMeta` carries one locale and one variable list through the whole run.",
        "width": 856,
        "height": 1000,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "Sticky Note1",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        -96
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 - Validate, repair once\n\nValid means no error-level diagnostics. The repair prompt points at the exact line and column, and the loop is capped at one round by wiring.",
        "width": 856,
        "height": 1000,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "Sticky Note2",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        832,
        -96
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 - Generate, then check what came out\n\n**Lint** judges each rendered document; **Uniqueness** judges the pool and reports a footprint. One template about one product lands near 0.5. Footprint Limit is 1 here, so the number only reports; set 0.15 to make it a gate.",
        "width": 856,
        "height": 1000,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "Sticky Note3",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1712,
        -96
      ]
    }
